    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Andy Pages** (70.07) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.66) as our offensive anchors. **Andy Pages** benefits from an elite matchup against Kochanowicz, where the favorable SP_xERA of 5.12 and a high-leverage lineup slot at #2 provide the highest ceiling on the team, despite the risk associated with a high-hold opposing pitcher. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** capitalizes on an advantageous platoon edge against Painter; his 0.379 xwOBA combined with a prime leadoff spot makes him a high-efficiency play for runs and total base volume. **Gunnar Henderson** (63.31) remains a must-start, as his aggressive approach against Fisher is bolstered by the pitcher's slow delivery, which creates a prime window for **Gunnar Henderson** to exploit the SB-scarce market we prioritize.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Brayan Rocchio** (41.36), who finished just outside the starting rotation. While **Brayan Rocchio** remains a serviceable depth piece, his #9 position in the lineup severely throttled his potential for R and RBI compared to the rest of the utility corps. We opted to prioritize the high-upside ceiling of **Nasim Nunez** (58.16), whose switch-hitting versatility and favorable matchup against E-Rod offered a superior projected floor. While **Dominic Smith** sits near the bottom of our starters with a 42.40 score, his inclusion is sustained by a favorable platoon edge; however, he remains a volatile piece of the lineup compared to the steady output expected from **Josh Jung** (53.90) and **Miguel Vargas** (59.01). \n\nManagement is monitoring **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.19) closely, as his matchup against the 3.62 xERA of Bradish represents the most significant SP-based hurdle for our core today. The 9% efficiency drop due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill underscores the importance of our high-speed outfielders, like **Sam Antonacci** and **Andy Pages**, to compensate for any potential stagnant run production from the corner infield. We are keeping **Coby Mayo** and **Nolan Schanuel** on standby, but given the 40.0 scoring floor, they remain strictly depth options unless late-breaking news forces a roster adjustment to our primary nine.",
